---
source: crates/pith-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: text
---
the pith kernel

Usage: pith [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  check    Elaborate the module at PATH and report its errors and warnings
  explore  Show what a module declares: types, rules, and which tier answers
  fmt      Write the canonical spelling of the module at PATH
  store    Inspect and admit content
  state    Inspect engine state
  gc       Report what a collection would reclaim
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --output <OUTPUT>  Output shape. Defaults to pretty on a TTY, plain otherwise [possible values: pretty, plain, json]
      --store <DIR>      Content store root. Defaults to $PITH_HOME/store [env: PITH_STORE=]
      --state <FILE>     Engine state root. Defaults to $PITH_HOME/state.db [env: PITH_STATE=]
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version
